<!-- SPEC ROWS — Ableton/pro-tool feel -->
<section class="section" id="features">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What's inside</span>
      <h2>Five instruments, one calm panel.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="specs">
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M12 7.5v5l3 2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">Live meter</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Your 5-hour and weekly Claude limits in the menu bar — exact or estimated — with a predictive "you'll hit your cap in ~2h at this burn" nudge so a lockout never surprises you mid-task.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 4l8 4-8 4-8-4 8-4Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M4 12l8 4 8-4M4 16l8 4 8-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">Multi-session Cockpit</span><span class="badge">New</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Run several <span class="mono">claude</span> projects at once — tabs, a project rail, or a mission-control overview — each showing real cost, model and RAM, under one shared binding limit and a memory-pressure gate that stops you oversaturating the Mac.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M13 3L5.5 13H11l-1 8 7.5-10H12l1-8Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">Autopilot</span><span class="badge">New</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Keeps Claude Code lean system-wide — a concise output-style and a usage statusline in every terminal — so every session spends fewer tokens by default. Fully reversible, any time.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M7 4v16M7 8h5M7 14h7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="17" cy="7" r="2.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">AI Optimizer</span><span class="badge">New</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Proposes a leaner, safer <span class="mono">CLAUDE.md</span> as a GitHub-style diff with a plain "why this is better" summary. You review every line before anything changes.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="7" cy="7" r="2.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="7" cy="17" r="2.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M9 8.6L19 17M9 15.4L19 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">Context trimmer &amp; audit</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Surgical context trimming, memory-pressure awareness and a config audit that flags what's quietly costing you — all measured, never guessed.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- OPTIMIZERS -->
<section class="section" id="optimize">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Fewer tokens</span>
      <h2>Optimizers that cut what you spend.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="specs">
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M5 7h14M5 12h10M5 17h6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">Output styles</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">One-click reply styles — Concise, or aggressive "Caveman" compression — applied to every <span class="mono">claude</span> session, terminal and Cockpit. Less prose per answer, the code and reasoning untouched.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 4.2-2.8 7.5-7 9-4.2-1.5-7-4.8-7-9V6l7-3Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">settings.json hardening</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Deterministic one-click fixes — deny blind reads of <span class="mono">.env</span>, <span class="mono">node_modules</span> and build output, set a cost-sane default model — each a reviewable diff, backed up before any change.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><rect x="3.5" y="5" width="9" height="7" rx="1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M5.5 10l2-2 2 2 1.5-1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M15 15h6M15 18h4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">Image → text on drop</span><span class="badge">New</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Drop a screenshot into a Cockpit session and Throttle OCRs it locally to text — a fraction of the tokens of a vision image. Hold <span class="mono">⌥</span> to keep it as an image.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="7" cy="7" r="2.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="7" cy="17" r="2.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M9 8.6L19 17M9 15.4L19 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">Context trimmer</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Strips re-charged base64 screenshots from past transcripts so <span class="mono">--resume</span> reloads light — reversible, the original backed up, the active session untouched.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M20 20l-4.2-4.2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">Searchable session memory</span><span class="badge">New</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Search your past <span class="mono">claude</span> sessions for context the window has lost — a dedicated Search window, plus an opt-in MCP server so Claude can search its own history too. Finds the right session even when you don't recall the exact word — searching "auth" also surfaces "login" and "token", entirely on-device.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="6" rx="1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="4" y="14" width="16" height="6" rx="1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="7" r="1" fill="currentColor"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="17" r="1" fill="currentColor"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">MCP manager &amp; memory hygiene</span><span class="badge">New</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Move any MCP server between Global, project-local and the shareable <span class="mono">.mcp.json</span>, enable, disable, add or remove one — each file backed up first. Zombie servers flagged with a real <span class="mono">list_tools</span> handshake; <span class="mono">MEMORY.md</span> indexed past Claude Code's 200-line / 25&nbsp;KB auto-load cap.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M12 12l4-2.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.4" fill="currentColor"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">Autopilot</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Keeps your Claude Code setup optimized system-wide, by default — concise replies and a live usage statusline on, dead memory from deleted projects archived. Every action reversible and logged; review or undo any of it in one place.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M4 8h6M4 8l2.5-2.5M4 8l2.5 2.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M20 16h-6M20 16l-2.5-2.5M20 16l-2.5 2.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M4 16h5M15 8h5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">Compress command output</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">A <span class="mono">PostToolUse</span> hook strips ANSI, dedups and trims verbose CLI output before Claude sees it — a green test run collapses to a line, errors always passed through raw. Fewer tokens per build, reversible.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-row reveal">
        <div class="sk"><span class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><ellipse cx="12" cy="6" rx="7" ry="2.6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M5 6v12c0 1.4 3.1 2.6 7 2.6s7-1.2 7-2.6V6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M9 13l-2 2 2 2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span><div><span class="st">Cache-bust attribution</span><span class="badge">New</span></div></div>
        <div class="sv">Shows <em>why</em> your prompt cache is being re-written — model swaps vs prefix churn — so the silent 10× re-reads that quietly inflate a session stop being invisible. Computed on-device from your own transcripts.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

